        "original_id": "26948afd-7497-533b-bdc7-e546f3ebf869",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luis Gianneo, Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, Rodolfo Arizaga, Marta Lambertini, Roberto Caamaño, Gerardo Gandini\n- Places: San Isidro, Buenos Aires\n- Organizations: Universidad Catolica Argentina\n- Roles: music educator, composer, pianist, music director\n\nFacts:\n- Ariel Ramírez was born on 4 September 1921 and was an Argentine composer, pianist, and music director.\n- Marta Lambertini was born in San Isidro, Buenos Aires.\n- Luis Gianneo worked as a music educator and taught composers including Ariel Ramírez, Juan Carlos Zorzi, Virtú Maragno, Pedro Ignacio Calderón, and Rodolfo Arizaga.\n- Marta Lambertini studied at the Universidad Catolica Argentina with Roberto Caamaño, Luis Gianneo, and Gerardo Gandini.\n- Marta Lambertini graduated from the Universidad Catolica Argentina in 1972.\n- Ariel Ramírez died on 18 February 2010.",
